course: dictionary
lesson: 6020
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, look at the context, which means the words and sentences around it. «Meditation means sitting quietly and focusing the mind, often on the breath.» The clues are sitting quietly and breath, so here meditation means calm, focused sitting.
explain: Dictionaries often list meanings with numbers, like 1), 2) and 3). Read each one and ask which one fits the sentence. «Marcus Aurelius kept a private notebook, the Meditations, to be honest with himself» needs a different meaning: here it is about careful thought written down, not sitting still.
explain: Check your choice by putting the meaning into the sentence in place of the word. If it still makes sense, you have probably chosen well. If it sounds silly, try the next meaning in the list.
fact: Meditation is a noun, and its plural is meditations.
fact: Meaning 1: sitting quietly and focusing your mind, for example on your breathing, to feel calm and relaxed.
fact: Meaning 2: a religious or spiritual practice of deep, quiet thought or prayer, as in Buddhism.
fact: Meaning 3 (formal): serious, careful thought about something, or a piece of writing with such thoughts.
fact: «Counting breaths from one to ten and starting again» is an old meditation technique, and losing count is normal.
exercise: «Counting breaths from one to ten is an old meditation technique.» What does meditation mean here? | *Sitting quietly and focusing your mind on your breathing | A loud party with music | A long journey to a faraway place | A test with lots of questions
exercise: «Many people still practise meditation, which comes from Buddhism and many other traditions.» Which meaning fits best? | A piece of writing with notes in the margin | *A religious or spiritual practice of deep, quiet thought or prayer | Running fast around a field | Sitting down for a rest after lunch
exercise: «Ella wrote a meditation on kindness for her school magazine.» What does meditation mean here? | *Serious, careful thought written down | Sitting still with her eyes closed | A type of cheap sweet | A loud school play
test: «Dad says his meditation app helps him feel calm before bed.» What does meditation mean here? | Running a marathon in the rain | *Sitting quietly and focusing the mind to feel calm and relaxed | A pile of old school books | A chef who cooks in a big kitchen
test: Which clue in «Monks practise meditation in their temple» tells you it is a religious practice? | Their | In | Practise | *Monks and temple
exam: «The Meditations of Marcus Aurelius were honest thoughts written in a notebook.» In this sentence, meditation means what? | Quiet sitting to relax | *Serious, careful thought, or writing with such thoughts | A religious prayer said at dinner | A type of drink
